                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "```\nipmi::RspType<\n    uint16_t,            // Next Record ID\n    std::vector<uint8_t> // SEL data\n> getSELEntry(...\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "storagehandler.cpp",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "storagehandler.cpp",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "@vernon.mauery@gmail.com\nWhy is `ipmi::message::Payload` not recommended here?\nAre there any conventions for when `ipmi::message::Payload` must be used?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "storagehandler.cpp",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "Payload is intended for variable type things where a single command can return a bunch of different types. It hides the response type, so it's not recommended unless there is no other way to do it. (get lan parameter is a good example)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "storagehandler.cpp",
                    "line": 367,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "nextRecordID needs to be placed at a more expansive scope (like line 348) so that it can be returned below."
                },
                {
                    "file": "storagehandler.cpp",
                    "line": 367,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "storagehandler.cpp",
                    "line": 379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "```\nreturn ipmi::responseSuccess(nextRecordID, buffer);\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "storagehandler.cpp",
                    "line": 379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
